- `packages/escher-driver` — one span per driver command, built at 2026-10-07-driver-command-spans (the route entry "Driver command spans", delivered): every call handed to `Session::run` opens one `tracing` span — target `escher_driver`, name `command`, level INFO, built by hand with `tracing::info_span!` (no `#[instrument]`), created and entered before `validate` and held until `run` returns, so a refusal `validate` returns is inside it — whose eight fields are each created unrecorded and recorded only where they apply: `verb`, the verb table's own word for a known verb, run or refused, never the caller's verb text and unrecorded for a verb the table lacks; `settled`, `busy` (the schema's word for the busy class, when the outcome carries one), `passes` (settle's pass count, when settle answered quiet — on a step that waited on a load, the settle that went quiet) and `added` · `removed` · `changed` (the three list lengths of the returned diff), from an acting verb's outcome; and `cause`, recorded at one site for every refusal `run` returns — one of the eight names `Cause::name` returns (`unknown-verb` · `malformed` · `not-found` · `stale` · `disabled` · `covered` · `off-screen` · `fonts-unavailable`, ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18), fixed class words holding nothing a call supplied, all eight returned by code today (`unknown-verb` and `malformed` by `validate`; `not-found`, `stale`, `disabled`, `covered`, `off-screen` and `fonts-unavailable` by the executor, the last before anything is painted when the held app has no font it can paint text with);
 `snapshot` and, since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, an accepted `screenshot` — whole, or by `id` — record `verb` alone (an element shot that crops to no pixel is refused `off-screen`), an accepted `lint` and a part read (`Outcome::Part`) record `verb` alone too, and a refused call records `verb` (when known) and `cause` and none of the other six; an accepted `advance` — accepted on every session (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18) — records `verb` and the acting fields like every acting verb, read by `stand_act_spans`' CRUD `advance` row (`Expect::Acts`); never fielded — `in_view`, `advanced_ms`, the screen text or its length, a part's number, the part count, a shot's image, its byte size or its `width` / `height`, a lint's findings or their count, the session's label, the record of ids, any argument, and any `Command`, `Call`, `ArgValue`, `Outcome`, `Refusal` or `Fault`: an argument fielded by its schema name, or a `Command` or an `Outcome` fielded with `Debug`, would print an id, typed text, an accessible name or a control's value (of the argument names only `text` is in the sink's scrub set, §8); the driver emits no event and installs no subscriber, so with none installed the span is disabled, under escher's sink it is one line per call at `info` or below (§6) and at the default `warn` it is filtered out before it is created; driven since 2026-10-14-quality-gates: `stand_act_spans` drives `press tab` through `Session::run` on an in-file fixture that mounts a freshly keyed element on every render, in both layout modes;
 the outcome reads not settled with `Busy::Render`, and the captured `command` line carries `settled=false` and `busy="render"`, no `passes` and no `cause` — six of the span's eight fields (`verb` · `settled` · `busy` · `added` · `removed` · `changed`) beside the sink's `span` · `message` · `time.busy` · `time.idle`, the three counts equal to the diff's lists — and the run asserts exactly one of its lines carried a busy class; the span keeps its eight fields (tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_spans.rs:555-567). Since 2026-10-10-driver-cli the span is also written by a hosted call: the `escher-session` host role decodes a wire `call` and runs it through `Session::run` and nothing else, so each hosted call is one closed `command` span under that binary's sink — measured, 3 lines for 3 calls at `RUST_LOG=trace` (`host_log`); a session-level verb (`start` · `status` · `stop`) or, since 2026-10-12-self-description, the tool-level `help` handed to `Session::run` is refused `unknown-verb` and its span still records the verb's table word; a call the schema refuses on the command line or in the client's `call` is answered there, reaches no session and opens no span; the span keeps its eight fields, a recording held or not, and an MCP call after which the recording ended is answered `isError` as `RecordingFailed`, its `tool_call` span ending `error` with `tool` and `ending` alone.
 Still observed absent — a span, an event or a `tracing` dependency in the settle wait itself, `Harness::settle` in `packages/blitz-test-harness`, and a span, an event or a field of its own in the driver's load wait over it (`settle_waiting`, bounded by `LOAD_WAIT`), which runs inside the call's `command` span and leaves its eight fields as they are, and a span, an event or a line of their own on `Session::start`, `Session::act`, `serve`, `start`, `attach`, `stop`, the wire — its `call` request and reply framing included — the client's `call`, `command_line` and its argv reader — its `help` ending, since 2026-10-12-self-description, reaching no session and opening no span — `describe()`, the `start` command's host spawn, the recording — `Session::recording_into`, `Session::recording_failed`, the recorder, `Check::from_bytes`, the replay `Check::replay` — each replayed step writing its own `command` span through `Session::run`, the replay adding none, `Replay` and `Change` holding only bools, a step index and closed key words — and the wire's `recording-failed` reply — and the host's idle expiry, which like a `stop` writes no record
 — and since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface `serve_mcp` itself and the rest of its protocol (`initialize` · `ping` · `tools/list` · a protocol error outside a tool call), which write no record either, and since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot `Harness::screenshot` / `screenshot_rect` in blitz-test-harness and the driver's private `image` encoder (`png`, `base64`), which print, panic and log nothing, and `Session::lint` itself, which the `lint` verb reaches inside its call's `command` span, opening none of its own, with blitz-dom's read-only `BaseDocument::text_extent` and `Harness::text_contrast`, the lint's contrast reader, and dioxus-native-dom's `Snapshot::text_parts`, the part read's cut, which open no span, emit no event and record no field, escher-driver keeping its 2 `info_span!` sites (packages/escher-driver/src/image.rs:3-37; packages/blitz-test-harness/src/screenshot.rs:37-103), and since 2026-10-13-stand-contrast-harness blitz-test-harness's contrast reader — `Harness::text_contrast` and the root re-exports `contrast_ratio` / `TextContrast`, its private sixth module `contrast` — which opens no span, emits no event, reads no env var, mutates nothing and prints, panics and logs nothing, the crate still taking no `tracing` (packages/blitz-test-harness/src/contrast.rs:13-23; packages/blitz-test-harness/src/contrast.rs:56-91): the span is `run`'s, beside the MCP server's `tool_call` (below) (packages/escher-driver/Cargo.toml:13-18; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:96-111; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:163-179; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:302-350; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:503-520; packages/escher-driver/src/command.rs:248; packages/blitz-test-harness/src/settle.rs:129-191;
 as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-session/report.md, the settle wait at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-settle-detection/report.md, the schema and its cause names at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-command-and-refusal-schema/report.md, the executor and the two causes it returned at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-act-by-id/report.md, the six it returned then at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-refusal-detection/report.md, the span at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md, the seventh, `fonts-unavailable`, and the shot's record at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-12-headless-screenshot/report.md)

- **escher-driver (in a process that installs escher's sink at `info` or below)**
  - one closed-span line per call to `Session::run`: INFO at target `escher_driver`, `span="command"`, with the recorded ones of `verb`, `cause`, `settled`, `busy`, `passes`, `added`, `removed`, `changed`, then `message="close"`, `time.busy`, `time.idle` — the verb table's twelve words (eight instance-level; the three session-level ones and the tool-level `help` only beside the cause `unknown-verb`), eight cause names (ratified by the founder, 2026-10-18), three busy-class words, bools and counts; since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot a shot's line is `span="command" verb="screenshot"` (with `cause` when refused) and holds no image byte, size or dimension — measured: 0 occurrences of the first 64 base64 characters of a shot in the `escher-session` host's and the `mcp` role's stderr at `trace`, under both builds (`host_log`, `mcp_log`; examples/seven_guis/tests/host_log.rs:398-411; examples/seven_guis/tests/mcp_log.rs:141-154); a lint's line is `span="command" verb="lint"` (with `cause` when refused) and holds no finding, id, bound or count — `host_log` and `mcp_log` each drive one `lint` at `trace` with 0 needles; a part read's line is `span="command" verb="snapshot"` (with `cause` when refused, a `part` outside 1 to 1000 refused `malformed`) and holds no part number, count, size or text — `host_log` and `mcp_log` each drive one part read at `trace` with 0 needles, and `host_log`'s fourth test reads a paged part of a served Cells screen through the host's own sink (`serve cells`, `snapshot --part 2`), 0 id and 0 name needles under both builds;
 no line at the default `warn`; the emitters are the two re-run children of `stand_act_spans`, in process, and since 2026-10-10-driver-cli the `escher-session` host — its wire (`v3`) carries `hello`, `stop` and `call` — a call after which the host's recording ended answered by the one fixed reply `recording-failed` —, and its host role writes one closed-span line per call at `info` or below (measured at `trace`: 3 lines for 3 calls);
 since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface also the `escher-session mcp` role and `serve_mcp` in process (`stand_mcp_tools`); `seven_guis_native` runs none (packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:96-111; packages/escher-driver/src/execute.rs:302-341; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md, the host's lines at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-driver-cli/report.md)
  - since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface, one closed-span line per MCP tool call: INFO at target `escher_driver`, `span="tool_call"`, with the recorded ones of `tool` (the table's word, one of its twelve, `help` among them since 2026-10-12-self-description and `screenshot` since 2026-10-12-headless-screenshot, and `lint`) and `ending` (`accepted` · `refused` · `error`), then `message="close"`, `time.busy`, `time.idle` — e.g. `span="tool_call" tool="start" ending="accepted" message="close"`; a `help` call's line reads `span="tool_call" tool="help" ending="accepted"` with no `command` line beside it; no line at the default `warn`; the emitters are the `escher-session mcp` role and `serve_mcp` in process; over one CRUD flow at `info` the role's stderr reads 9 lines built alone and 10 built with the workspace — the tenth `INFO blitz_dom::document … message=[redacted]` — with 5 `tool_call` and 3 `command` lines in each (packages/escher-driver/src/mcp.rs:118-121; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-mcp-surface/report.md, read on the hand-run role, 2026-10-11); re-measured at 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep, 9 built alone and 11 built with the workspace — the `blitz_dom::document` INFO line now printing twice — the 5 `tool_call` and 3 `command` lines unchanged, needles 0 (as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep/evidence/log-counts.md)
